      "value": "Wills, Larry Carter; Warren, Steve; Zarrilli, Tom; Shaw, Russell; Raby, Mike; Wantuck, Karen E.; Groger, John J.; Krischer, David E.; Morris, Sandra Germon;"
    },
    {
      "controlledVocab": false,
      "controlledVocabList": null,
      "key": "biogra",
      "label": "Biographical/Historical note",
      "searchable": true,
      "value": "Creative Loafing was started in 1972 by Deborah and Elton (Chick) Eason and expanded to other cities in the 1980s and 1990s under Creative Loafing Inc. It went through various ownerships starting in 2009, before being purchased by Ben Eason, son of the founders, bringing the publication back to the family as Creative Loafing, LLC, in 2017. Creative Loafing Inc. was once the nation's second largest publisher of alternative weeklies."
    },
    {
      "controlledVocab": false,
      "controlledVocabList": null,
      "key": "descri",
      "label": "Description",
      "searchable": true,
      "value": "The July 12th, 1975 issue of Creative Loafing has front page articles on Cobb County mass transit and a theater production, and includes articles on events in Atlanta, music, books, and the arts.  Also included is the July 8th, 1975 issue of Spirit of the Times, which includes articles on schools, the Inman Baseball League, credit contracts, and a road-side grocer."
    },
